# Safety at Home — environment variables
#
# All values are set in Coolify. Never commit real values to the repo.
# Phase 1 needs no env vars at all — this file documents what is coming.

# Public base URL of the site, used for canonical URLs and metadata.
# Example format: https://safety.thurrock.gov.uk
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=

# --- Phase 6 (Postgres + Prisma) ---
# Postgres connection string for Prisma. If unset, the site still runs:
# feedback is not stored, the damp report form falls back to a pre-filled
# email, and the address lookup says it is not available.
# Example format: postgresql://user:password@host:5432/dbname
# DATABASE_URL=

# ARC asbestos register feed. A URL that returns JSON: an array of
# { id, uprn, location, material, condition, lastInspected }. Read by
# `npm run arc:sync` (scheduled job), never by the web app at request time.
# ARC_FEED_URL=
# Optional bearer token sent as Authorization: Bearer <token>.
# ARC_FEED_TOKEN=
